## Flutter app configuration — copy to `.env` at the repo root.
##
## Read by lib/config/app_config.dart, which prefers this file and falls back
## to `--dart-define` for the same name. A missing `.env` is not an error: the
## app starts, and every value below falls back as described.
##
## IMPORTANT: `.env` is listed under `flutter: assets:` in pubspec.yaml, so it
## is bundled into the APK/IPA and ships to every device. Anything in here is
## readable by anyone who unzips the build. Public, RLS-protected values only —
## the service_role key, the Groq key and the Modal secrets belong in
## backend/.env, which never leaves the server.

## Supabase — the project URL and the *anon* (publishable) key.
## Safe to ship: RLS grants anon+authenticated select on the public catalogue
## and nothing else. Project Settings > API in the dashboard.
## No fallback — auth and every catalogue read fail without these.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

## The backend/server-node instance the app talks to. No trailing slash.
##
## Leave it unset and the app guesses per platform:
##   Android emulator          http://10.0.2.2:8000  (the host's loopback)
##   iOS simulator / desktop   http://localhost:8000
##
## Neither guess works on a *physical* device — localhost there is the phone.
## Set your machine's LAN address and keep the phone on the same Wi-Fi:
##   API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.42:8000
## Find it with `ipconfig` (Windows) or `ipconfig getifaddr en0` (macOS).
API_BASE_URL=

## Whether the AR mascot hunt spawns near the device's own position instead of
## a route stop's real coordinates.
##
## Defaults to true (unset counts as true) because there is no way to stand at
## the pilot city's actual POIs during ordinary development — on it, the whole
## hunt loop can be exercised by walking around wherever you are. Only the
## literal string `false` turns it off. Also toggleable live from Settings, so
## this is just the value the app starts with.
AR_TESTING_MODE=true
